ml: similar to show heading and back button.\n\nImplement minimal styling.\n\nNow apply patches via exec_command: use bash -c \"cat \u003e server.js \u003c\u003c'EOF' ... EOF\". Ensure proper quoting.\n\nLet's proceed step by step.\n\n","id":"rs_561775","summary":[{"text":"We need to fix previous submission. The error: tool call format invalid because we used apply_patch with raw string containing newlines and quotes; need correct JSON escaping. The tool expects exec_command? Actually we need to apply patches using git? There is no apply_patch tool defined. Usually we use exec_command to run git commands and apply patches via cat \u003e file. We'll need to create server.js and other files, commit them.\n\nGoal: implement task 001 as described.\n\nWe need to create server.js, public/index.html, public/project.html, maybe a small client JS. Use only node built-in modules, sqlite. Node 22. Use ES modules.\n\nImplement minimal UI satisfying requirements: index page with heading Workboard, textbox label Project name, button Create project, list of projects with rows data-testid=\"project-row\", name, button Open project.\n\nAlert visible when blank.\n\nProject page: heading with project name, button Projects to go back.\n\nPersist data in SQLite DB_PATH.\n\nServe health endpoint.\n\nNeed npm start script: likely in package.json \"start\": \"node server.js\". Ensure package.json exists.\n\nWe must commit all changes and ensure git status clean.\n\nWe need to run commands to create files, add them, commit. Use exec_command with proper commands.\n\nLet's implement.\n\nImplementation plan:\n\nCreate server.js as ES module. Use node:http, node:path, node:fs/promises, node:sqlite, node:sqlite3.\n\nSet up DB, create table.\n\nDefine routes:\n\n- GET /health JSON.\n\n- API: GET /api/projects list, POST /api/projects create, GET /api/projects/:id.\n\n- Serve static files from public directory.\n\n- For any other, 404.\n\nAdd package.json with \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": {\"start\":\"node server.js\"}.\n\nCreate public/index.html with simple HTML and client JS inline or separate file.\n\nSimplify: embed script in index.html that fetches /api/projects, renders list, handles create.\n\nProject page project.html: similar to show heading and back button.\n\nImplement minimal styling.\n\nNow apply patches via exec_command: use bash -c \"cat \u003e server.js \u003c\u003c'EOF' ... EOF\". Ensure proper quoting.\n\nLet's proceed step by step.\n\n","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":456,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

